From: The Surface Duo port <none@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] shell: a display with a seam shows no home surface

On a display with a seam the home surface is never seen: it has no home bar
there (patch 0013) and the port's dock holds the applications. Shown anyway,
it answered the last window closing by redrawing all of itself - 2784x5952 on
the Surface Duo - two or three times, as the overview gave up its running
activities and the home's handle was resized. On this phone's GPU every such
partial upload of a shared-memory buffer takes the slow path, ~20 ms, and the
closing window's own fade lost 3-4 frames to it: 7.3% of its frames against
1.9% with this.

The shell's overview-visible property, bound to the home's visibility, is set
false on such a display.
---
--- a/src/shell.c
+++ b/src/shell.c
@@ -711,6 +711,17 @@
                                                    phosh_wayland_get_zphoc_layer_shell_effects_v1 (wl),
                                                    monitor));
   g_object_bind_property (self, "overview-visible", priv->home, "visible", G_BINDING_SYNC_CREATE);
+  /* On a display with a seam the home surface is never seen: it has no home
+   * bar there (home.c) and the shell's dock holds the applications. Shown
+   * anyway, it redrew the whole of itself - 2784x5952 on this phone - two
+   * or three times as the last window closed, ~20 ms of upload each, and
+   * the window's own fade lost 3-4 frames to it (#147). */
+  {
+    GdkRectangle seam;
+
+    if (phosh_layout_manager_get_seam (priv->layout_manager, &seam))
+      g_object_set (self, "overview-visible", FALSE, NULL);
+  }
 
   g_signal_connect_swapped (priv->top_panel,
                             "activated",
